**Verdict:** [Three-Stone Tapered Baguette at $4,277 lab total](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/three-stone-tapered-baguette-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-4-ct-tw-item-203640?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the strongest value in this list. You get the Extension Effect, a clean classic look, and certified quality with 1/4 ct tw of side stones. For the statement buyer, the [Five-Stone at $8,787 lab](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/five-stone-tapered-baguette-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-3-4-ct-tw-item-203694?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is a completely different category of ring — the baguette presence becomes the design, not just the frame.

> **Farzana says:** "The most common mistake I see with baguette rings is buying the side stones too small. Tiny baguettes next to a 1ct+ radiant look lost — they read as scratches rather than stones. The Three-Stone Tapered at 1/4 ct tw is the minimum I'd recommend for a 1ct center. If you're going 1.5ct or above, look at the Five-Stone."

